Quickly familiarize with the workflows, policies, and requirements of each assigned department;
Provide administrative support, including data entry, scheduling, correspondence, and record management;
Ensure smooth day-to-day operations by proactively identifying and resolving administrative bottlenecks;
Transition seamlessly between departments, maintaining a high level of professionalism and efficiency;
Adapt to varying priorities, tasks, and team dynamics depending on the department's unique needs;
Propose and implement improvements to administrative processes, ensuring sustainability and consistency;
Share best practices across departments when applicable;
Provide assistance and support to team members in efforts of achieving overall team goals.
Requirements
Grade 12 or equivalent (Essential);
Minimum of 1 year experience in a general administrative or similar role (Essential);
Familiarity with office tools like scheduling tools and filing systems;
Ability to quickly learn new software, systems and various processes;
Knowledge of Microsoft Office (Word, Excel and Outlook);
Strong organisational skills and attention to detail;
Good written and verbal communication skills;
Strong time-management and multitasking abilities;
Problem solving.

ABOUT THE ROLE:
This role is a permanent full-time position.
As an Superintendent Production, you will be responsible for managing and ensure successful production execution processes, while maintaining safety and costs. .
Other key responsibilities include, but aren’t limited to:
Manage mining operations and processes;
Monitor daily achievement of targets;
Ensuring that the Load & Haul team supports and enables the delivery of areas planned to be mined for the production month;
Embrace diversity and promote inclusion;
Safely deliver volume targets;
Sign-off and manage the execution of the Monthly Plans;
Assist in implementing and assuring project work meets quality requirements;
Responsible for safety and improvements in their areas of responsibility;
Support Safety and Health initiatives and campaigns .
ABOUT YOU:
You will have experience and demonstrate capability in the following:
Minimum of 5 years’ experience in Production & Mining environment of which 2 years must be in a Line Leadership role;
Experience of underground Load & Haul requirements.
Qualifications for this role are:
Mine Overseer Certificate of Competency OR Mine Manager Certificate;
Degree or Diploma Mining Engineering will be advantageous;
Valid drivers license.
